1
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:29,333
How much can a man take...before he gives back?

2
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:52,666
Lock Up is a action, crime, drama film directed by John Flynn.

3
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Frank Leone is nearing the end of his prison term for a relatively minor crime.

4
00:25:33,333 --> 00:25:39,333
Just before he is paroled, however, Warden Drumgoole takes charge.

5
00:31:56,666 --> 00:32:02,666
Drumgoole was assigned to a hell-hole prison after his administration was publicly humiliated by
Leone, and has now arrived on the scene to ensure that Leone never sees the light of day.

6
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Frank Leone, played by Sylvester Stallone.

7
00:44:43,333 --> 00:44:49,333
Warden Drumgoole, played by Donald Sutherland.

8
00:51:06,666 --> 00:51:12,666
Captain Meissner, played by John Amos.

9
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Chink Weber, played by Sonny Landham.

10
01:03:53,333 --> 01:03:59,333
Dallas, played by Tom Sizemore.

11
01:10:16,666 --> 01:10:22,666
Eclipse, played by Frank McRae.

12
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
Lock Up is a 1989 American prison action film directed by John Flynn, and starring
Sylvester Stallone, Donald Sutherland, John Amos and Tom Sizemore.

13
01:23:03,333 --> 01:23:09,333
It was released in the United States on August 4, 1989.

14
01:29:26,666 --> 01:29:32,666
Stallone later said it was "Not a film that was produced and performed with enough
maturity to really make a significant impact on the audience or my career.

15
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
And that's the truth".

16
01:42:13,333 --> 01:42:19,333
The film explores themes of prison, self sacrifice,
jail guard, car mechanic, prison warden.

17
01:48:36,666 --> 01:48:42,666
The tone is emotional and intense.
